          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"2-my-plan-before-ai\">2. My Plan Before AI</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Part A:</span>\n<div class=\"language-teratermmacro highlight\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span>.<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">List</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">every</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">town</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">in</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">the</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">county</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">(</span><span class=\"nv\">will</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">pagination</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">to</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">confirm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">collected</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">all</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">of</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">them</span><span class=\"ss\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span>.<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">Fiscal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">year</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2026</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">history</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">each</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">town</span>.<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">Figures</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">needed</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">each</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">town</span><span class=\"err\">'s history: average home value, residential tax rate and average bill.</span>\n\n<span class=\"err\">    3. Is the town\u2019s average home value within their budget? And Is the town\u2019s average bill within their tax limit?</span>\n\n<span class=\"err\">    4. Average bill lowest to highest</span>\n\n<span class=\"err\">    5. Table containing every town in Middlesex where the price and property tax meet their budget. Columns: town, average home value, residential tax rate, average bill.</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Part B:</span>\n<div class=\"language-scdoc highlight\"><pre><span></span><code>    1. get_towns(county) \u2192 in: county name, out: list of town records &amp; get_town_history(dor_code, year) \u2192 in: dor_code + fiscal year, out: that town's history record\n\n    2. /ma/towns &amp; /ma/towns/{dor_code}/history\n\n    3. Pagination: comparing total and pages\n\n4. The average home value times the tax rate divided by 1,000 should come out close to the average bill. Tax rates are quoted per $1,000 of value.\n</code></pre></div></span>"
